---
---

<div class="interactive-workflow" data-interactive-tabs aria-label="Interactive workflow sandbox">
  <div class="tab-nav" role="tablist">
    <button class="tab-btn is-active" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-tab-target="tab-delegate">
      <strong>1. Delegate</strong>
      <span>Dynamic routing to specialized capability</span>
    </button>
    <button class="tab-btn" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-tab-target="tab-compare">
      <strong>2. Compare</strong>
      <span>Multi-candidate parallel evaluation</span>
    </button>
    <button class="tab-btn" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-tab-target="tab-verify">
      <strong>3. Verify</strong>
      <span>Executable evidence & automated testing</span>
    </button>
    <button class="tab-btn" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-tab-target="tab-iterate">
      <strong>4. Iterate</strong>
      <span>Autonomous correction loops</span>
    </button>
  </div>

  <div class="tab-content">
    <div class="tab-panel is-active" data-tab-panel="tab-delegate" role="tabpanel">
      <div class="run-card__header">
        <span>Assignment Resolver</span>
        <strong>Target Resolved: Codex Worker on MacBook Host</strong>
      </div>
      <div class="terminal-panel">
<code is:raw>// Cloud evaluates task constraints and routes to authorized Host
const target = await scheduler.resolveTarget({
  task: "Implement D1 durable transaction adapter",
  workspace: "ws_production",
  requiredCapabilities: ["filesystem", "d1_sqlite"]
});
// → Dispatched to MacBook Host (Latency: 24ms, Status: Ready)</code>
      </div>
      <p>Tasks declare execution requirements. Conclave Cloud matches them against online Hosts, installed Workers, and authorized Accounts without hardcoding model locations.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tab-panel" data-tab-panel="tab-compare" role="tabpanel" hidden>
      <div class="run-card__header">
        <span>Multi-Worker Synthesis</span>
        <strong>Evaluating Candidate Implementations</strong>
      </div>
      <div class="terminal-panel">
<code is:raw>[Candidate A - OpenAI Worker]
+ Implements batch atomic statements with retry backoff.
[Candidate B - Claude Worker]
+ Implements write-ahead journal with rollback hooks.

// Synthesis Worker identifies edge cases in Candidate B
// Recommends: Merge atomic retry with rollback hooks</code>
      </div>
      <p>When solving hard problems, run diverse model capabilities in parallel. Conclave synthesizes their strengths and highlights architectural trade-offs.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tab-panel" data-tab-panel="tab-verify" role="tabpanel" hidden>
      <div class="run-card__header">
        <span>Independent Verification</span>
        <strong>Deterministic Proof Collection</strong>
      </div>
      <div class="terminal-panel">
<code is:raw>✓ Test suite executed: 44 test files, 326 passed (100%)
✓ Architecture boundary guard: 0 violations
✓ Security audit: Zero credential leaks detected
✓ Artifact generated: dist/d1-adapter.mjs (SHA256 verified)</code>
      </div>
      <p>Never trust natural-language claims that "it works". Conclave executes real tests, collects machine evidence, and ensures deterministic completion.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tab-panel" data-tab-panel="tab-iterate" role="tabpanel" hidden>
      <div class="run-card__header">
        <span>Correction Loop</span>
        <strong>Autonomous Finding Remediation</strong>
      </div>
      <div class="terminal-panel">
<code is:raw>[Finding Detected] Reviewer noted race condition on lock release
[Auto-Correction] Task dispatched to Worker with review findings
[Patch Applied] Lock lease timeout bounded to 5000ms
[Reverification] Test suite passed cleanly on 2nd cycle.</code>
      </div>
      <p>When a reviewer or test finds an issue, Conclave feeds the exact findings back into a focused correction task and reverifies the result.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
